{"tool_name":"cpi-igae","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"cpi-igae","home":"https://github.com/wanxiaozhe/CPI-IGAE","license":"Not licensed","summary":"An inductive graph neural network model for compound-protein interaction prediction based on a homogeneous graph.","addition_date":"2022-06-24T14:37:01.968822Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T16:01:35.696464Z","tool_type":["Workbench","Workflow"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:cpi-igae","credit":[{"email":"lixutong@simm.ac.cn","name":"Mingyue Zheng","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"myzheng@simm.ac.cn","name":"Xutong Li","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3927"},{"term":"Protein interaction prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2492"},{"term":"Virtual screening","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3938"}]}],"name":"CPI-IGAE","owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bib/bbac073","metadata":{"abstract":"Identifying the potential compound\u2013protein interactions (CPIs) plays an essential role in drug development. The computational approaches for CPI prediction can reduce time and costs of experimental methods and have benefited from the continuously improved graph representation learning. However, most of the network-based methods use heterogeneous graphs, which is challenging due to their complex structures and heterogeneous attributes. Therefore, in this work, we transformed the compound\u2013protein heterogeneous graph to a homogeneous graph by integrating the ligand-based protein representations and overall similarity associations. We then proposed an Inductive Graph AggrEgator-based framework, named CPI-IGAE, for CPI prediction. CPI-IGAE learns the low-dimensional representations of compounds and proteins from the homogeneous graph in an end-to-end manner. The results show that CPI-IGAE performs better than some state-of-the-art methods. Further ablation study and visualization of embeddings reveal the advantages of the model architecture and its role in feature extraction, and some of the top ranked CPIs by CPI-IGAE have been validated by a review of recent literature. The data and source codes are available at https://github.com/wanxiaozhe/CPI-IGAE.","authors":[{"name":"Fu Z."},{"name":"Jiang H."},{"name":"Li X."},{"name":"Liu X."},{"name":"Tan X."},{"name":"Wan X."},{"name":"Wang D."},{"name":"Wu X."},{"name":"Zheng M."}],"citationCount":14,"date":"2022-05-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Briefings in Bioinformatics","title":"An inductive graph neural network model for compound\u2013protein interaction prediction based on a homogeneous graph"},"pmcid":"PMC9310259","pmid":"35275993"}],"topic":[{"term":"Drug development","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3373"},{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Medicinal chemistry","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0209"},{"term":"Molecular modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2275"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"CPI-IGAE","home":"https://bio.tools/cpi-igae","license":"Not licensed","summary":"An inductive graph neural network model for compound-protein interaction prediction based on a homogeneous graph.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:cpi-igae/workbench/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":false,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":12,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2026"},{"count":2,"year":"2024"},{"count